## Criteria and verdicts

{% include 'shared/_criterion_verification_procedure.j2' %}

Use one stable `PA-###` item per criterion in `## Criterion Verdicts`.
Include `Plan-level:` or a step reference, then `Criterion:`, `Expected
observation:`, `Observation:`, `Proposed revision:`, `Verdict:`,
`Evidence:`, `Location:`, and `Cost:`. `completed` requires every criterion
to be `met` with evidence and no counterexample found. For `request_changes`
or `failed`, mirror each localized non-met verdict in `## What Came Up
Short`; each mirrored finding carries its `Proposed revision:` so the
planner can apply it on the next pass, or rebut it with evidence. Do not
add a `## How To Fix` section. A `not evaluable` criterion requires
`failed`.

